<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eunostos of Soloi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 4th century BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eunostos was the last king of Soloi in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>, ruling at the end of the 4th century BCE as an ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-i-soter">Ptolemy I</a>. He married Eirene, a daughter of Ptolemy, which bound his small kingdom to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemaic-kingdom">Ptolemaic dynasty</a>. After his reign Soloi was absorbed into Ptolemaic Cyprus, as were the island's other city-kingdoms.</p></div>
